lf, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n```\n\nNote: `record.message` — set by super().format(). Good.\n\nEdge: when truncation occurs, the tail may include... fine.\n\nOne nuance: keep_full_message check happens before computing getMessage, so no overhead. Good.\n\nNow stats_logger edit. Let me read lines 110-135 to confirm exact text of _log_worker (evidence gives it, sha matches current). Then edit `logger.info(m)` → `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nLet me do all edits in one action: replace_text_batch for logger.py, and for stats_logger.py.\n\nFor logger.py import of envs — where? Add after `from types import TracebackType\\n\\n`. Hmm, isort style: local imports after stdlib. Insert:\n\n```\nfrom types import TracebackType\n\nfrom deepinfer.environ import envs\n```\n\nThat's a distinct edit anchor: `from types import TracebackType\\n` → `from types import TracebackType\\n\\nfrom deepinfer.environ import envs\\n`.\n\nLet's write."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8436,"completion_tokens":4227,"total_tokens":12663,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3204},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":4340},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}